@dsh-external/dsh-session-folder README · 1. 会话：打开项目目录：**右键会话列表里的任意会话行**（或照旧点行尾的 `…`）→ 弹出该会话自己的操作菜单 → **「在资源管理器中打开」**（位于「归档会话」之后、「复制 Session ID」之前）。

右键触发的是**同一份宿主菜单**（只是多了一种打开方式），所以置顶 / 重命名 / 分叉 / 归档 / 复制 Session ID 全都在，不会出现两份不一致的菜单。

打开的目标是该会话 summary 的 `cwd`，也就是它所属工作区的目录。

@dsh-external/dsh-session-folder README · 兼容性：- DSH `0.2.1-rc` 系列（依赖 `sidebar.workspaces.session.menu.item` / `shell.overlay` 槽位、`session.openWorkspacePath` Remote，以及 `ctx.sessions` / `ctx.uiWorkspace` 服务）。
- 需要「能把路径交给本机桌面」的部署：DSH Desktop，或本机运行的 Web 版；纯远程/无桌面环境下打开类操作会失败并给出提示。
- 不占用模型上下文：这是纯浏览器界面插件，不注册工具、不写会话。

@dsh-external/dsh-session-folder README · 3. Web link → context menu：> Note: user-message text is plain (`UserTextRun` renders `<span>{text}</span>`, no Markdown or link
> parsing), so a URL typed by the user is not an anchor and has no link menu today. Only Markdown links in
> assistant messages go through the link menu.

@dsh-external/dsh-session-folder README · 3. Web link → context menu：**Image links (`.png` and friends) work too**: the host drops `title` from a Markdown link that points at
an image so it can show the inline preview, leaving only the link text in the DOM. The **exact target is read
from the link component's own React props** (it is built from `{ file: { path } }`, and `file.path` is the
target as written in the markdown), so a link whose label differs from its path still opens the right file;
only when those props are unavailable does the plugin fall back to a label that looks like a file name.

@dsh-external/dsh-session-folder README · Uninstall：Settings → Plugins → disable / remove, or
`dsh plugin --profile <profile> remove @dsh-external/dsh-session-folder` and drop the row from `dsh.profile.bundles`.

---

@dsh-external/dsh-session-folder README · Compatibility：- DSH `0.2.1-rc` line (needs the `sidebar.workspaces.session.menu.item` / `shell.overlay` slots, the
  `session.openWorkspacePath` Remote, and the `ctx.sessions` / `ctx.uiWorkspace` services).
- Requires a deployment that can hand paths to a local desktop (DSH Desktop, or a locally run Web build);
  open actions fail with a notice otherwise.
- Model-neutral: a browser UI plugin with no tools and no session writes.
